  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>daptomycin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC code:</td><td>J01XX09</td></tr><tr><td>model:</td><td>two compartments, IV dosing <small>(PK_2C)</small></td></tr><tr><td>source:</td><td>Lou Y et al. 2021</td></tr><tr><td>population:</td><td>kidney transplant recipients</td></tr><tr><td>measured compound:</td><td>daptomycin</td></tr><tr><td>review:</td><td>curated candidate</td></tr><tr><td>record page:</td><td><a href=\"https://pharmacolibrary.github.io/#/drugs/drug_daptomycin/Daptomycin_Lou2021_reference\">pharmacolibrary-docs</a></td></tr></table><h4>Parameters as reported in the paper</h4><table border=1 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=2><tr><th>parameter</th><th>value</th><th>unit</th><th>meaning</th></tr><tr><td>clearance</td><td>0.316</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>CL</small></td></tr><tr><td>central volume of distribution</td><td>6.04</td><td>L</td><td><small>V1</small></td></tr><tr><td>intercompartmental clearance</td><td>2.31</td><td>L/h</td><td><small>Q</small></td></tr><tr><td>peripheral volume of distribution</td><td>2.46</td><td>L</td><td><small>V2</small></td></tr></table><h4>About daptomycin</h4><p>Daptomycin is an antibiotic used to treat serious bacterial infections, mainly those caused by gram-positive bacteria such as staphylococci, including skin infections, bacteremia, and infective endocarditis. It is an approved medicine authorised in the European Union and is generally used in hospital settings for severe infections.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q418747\">Wikidata Q418747</a> and the WHO ATC classification and the EMA medicines list; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Daptomycin\">Daptomycin</a>.</p><h4>References</h4><ol><li><p>Lou Y et al. (2021). Population pharmacokinetics and individual analysis of daptomycin in kidney transplant recipients. <i>European journal of pharmaceutical sciences : official journal of the European Federation for Pharmaceutical Sciences 162:105818</i>. DOI:<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejps.2021.105818\">10.1016/j.ejps.2021.105818</a> PUBMED:<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33771717\">33771717</a></p></li></ol></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Lou_2021: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"),
